    "description": "Tsehai Young Leaders Fellowship- Paid Whiz Kids Workshop | Tsehai Loves Learning | Tsehai for Families How much responsibility could you earn if someone gave you the chance to prove yourself? You’re early in your career. You learn fast. You notice problems, figure things out and follow through. You want meaningful work—and the opportunity to become someone a team can depend on. We’re looking for you. At Whiz Kids Workshop, we’re building Tsehai 2.0: a platform that helps caregivers develop practical skills, demonstrate their competence and connect with families and employers. Yes, you guessed it. It is an extension of ፀሐይ መማር ትወዳለች🥰 We’re opening a paid Tsehai Young Leaders Fellowship to develop people who can run, improve and eventually lead the systems behind that mission. What you’ll learn and do You’ll work across seven connected systems: Registration and onboarding: help people start successfully. Skill assessment: protect quality and turn evidence into sound decisions. Caregiver portfolio and employer services: create value for both sides. Learner support: identify barriers and help people move forward. Team operations: manage priorities, capacity and continuous flow. Talent development: help others learn, improve and earn responsibility. Content marketing and advertising: attract the right caregivers and employers to Tsehai. You’ll learn to identify what limits results, question unnecessary requirements, simplify processes and measure whether your changes work. Your application is where the learning begins This fellowship uses a hands-on selection process. We’re looking for exceptional early-career talent with the potential to lead. Each stage introduces you to Tsehai’s mission, work and daily practices through short courses, videos and practical assignments. As you advance, you’ll submit practical work and use feedback to improve it. Start preparing as soon as you open the application. Set aside time to read the linked materials, watch the videos, reflect on what you’ve learned and organize your submission before each deadline. Your application is your first opportunity to show how you learn and put that learning into practice. Application section The selection process includes four practical assessments. Each stage introduces you to how Tsehai works and gives you a chance to apply what you learn. Open the application early so you have time to review the materials and prepare a thoughtful response. Stage 1 : Mission and first signal. Review six child development concepts, respond to a caregiving scenario and reflect on how your experiences and skills could contribute to Tsehai. Your submission includes a short essay and response in Amharic. Stage 2 : Learn through practice. If invited, read the reflection questions before starting Modules 1 and 2 of Tsehai’s Caregiver Course on Tsehai Telegram. Practise Responsive caregiving with a child under 8, submit the required evidence and apply any coaching feedback you receive. In your final reflection, explain what you learned, where a learner might get stuck and one small improvement you would test. Stages 3 and 4 : Apply your judgment. Work through one case connecting Tsehai’s seven systems, then complete an observed operating assessment. Candidates who advance will be invited to a final interview. Before applying, confirm that you can arrange safe caregiving practice with a child under 8 through family or trusted friends, with permission from the child’s parent or guardian. Obtain their permission before recording any practice. Allow time to review the materials, complete the activities and submit your work by each stage’s deadline.",
