    "datePosted": "2026-11-10T13:32:47.000Z",
    "description": "Our Profile People in Need is a non-governmental, non-profit organization founded on the ideals of humanism, freedom, equality and solidarity. We consider human dignity and freedom to be fundamental values. We believe that people anywhere in the world should have the right to make decisions about their lives and to share the rights expressed in the Universal Declaration of Human Rights. The People in Need organization was established in 1992 by a group of Czech war correspondents who were no longer satisfied with merely relaying information about ongoing conflicts and began sending out aid. It gradually became established as a professional humanitarian organization striving to provide aid in troubled regions and support adherence to human rights around the world. Throughout our over 25 years of its existence, People in Need has become one of the biggest non-profit organizations in Central Europe. In addition to humanitarian aid and human rights, it now also targets education and helps people living in social exclusion. We are part of Alliance 2015, a strategic network of seven European non-governmental organizations engaged in humanitarian aid and development projects. This collaboration increases effectiveness, both in working in the target countries and in campaigns aimed at influencing the attitudes of politicians and the general public in Europe. In our over 20 years operation in Ethiopia, has focused on projects in five main areas of interest: Education and Social protection, Environment, Livelihood and Agriculture, Water, sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) and Emergency programs. More information at www.peopleinneed.cz or HERE . PIN would like to invite energetic, disciplined, responsible female Finance intern applicant to work under Finance department. Length of internship : for 3 months Number required : 1 (one) Duration of the assignment until March 31,2027 Transport allowance :6500 birr Job Role: Under the general guidance and supervision of the finance officer, the Intern will learn in assisting planning, coordination and follow up of grass root level activities for finance department. Technical areas of learning /for interns to involve Preparing of cash payment voucher, Invoice, withholding tax payment voucher. Filing and arranging of Invoice, cash and other finance related documents. Follow-up on cash disbursement process at cash disbursement spot. Closely working with SFO and FO to support & to build capacity in managing finance related issues. Scanning & archiving of all finance related documents. Any other finance related tasks as required and assigned. Project related areas of learning/for interns to involve Attain adequate results in proper quality and in time Provide finance officers with weekly plans and reports of activities achieved. The reports shall be submitted every Thursday morning and will contain a shortlist of activities achieved in the past week and activities planned for the next one Assist the finance team when a need arises TEAM REQUIREMENTS Maintain good personal relations in the team Actively collaborate with PIN’s other ongoing finance team members in the finance operation areas when required Any other tasks as requested by the line managers PIN stipulates the right to assign the Intern any other kind of work derived from his/her specialization. In case of urgent work and such like the Intern may be asked to work overtime as well as during public and other holidays. In case that larger amount of different tasks is to be fulfilled by the Intern at the same time, the Intern shall accomplish the urgent and more important duties first. Furthermore, the Intern is responsible for: Correctness and completeness of information acquired Ensuring timely and effective implementation of finance activities and meeting set results Prompt provision of all relevant information to finance officers/ finance unit Manger Archiving of all entrusted and acquired documents in proper manner The Intern is obligated not to purvey any information concerning any of PIN activities to outsiders (including former PIN employees, who may no more be informed about current process in PIN). PIN is a relief and development organization whose aim is to help and assist needy people. The Intern’s position within the institution requires contacts with outside; he or she therefore conveys a certain image of the PIN. PIN expects its interns to behave in appropriate manners at all times and in all places. All members of staff and interns should ensure their attitudes correspond to PIN principles, both during and after working hours. The Intern takes over the responsibility for all entrusted material or cash. The Intern is obligated to cover all damages or losses caused by his carelessness. The Agreement of Liability of Assets has been signed separately.",
