    "description": "JOB VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT Position Title: Communications and Digital Media Specialist Organization: Nexus of National Humanitarian Actors in Ethiopia (Nexus Ethiopia) Duty Station: Addis Ababa, Ethiopia Employment Type: Full-time Reports to: Executive Director Salary: Based on the organization's salary scale and applicable employment policies Application Deadline: Ten working days from the date of publication About Nexus Ethiopia Nexus of National Humanitarian Actors in Ethiopia (Nexus Ethiopia) is a national civil society organization committed to strengthening the resilience of vulnerable communities through integrated humanitarian, development, and peacebuilding (HDP Nexus) interventions. The organization works with communities, government institutions, civil society organizations, and development partners to address humanitarian needs, promote sustainable development, strengthen local capacities, and advance peacebuilding and social cohesion. Nexus Ethiopia is committed to locally led development, institutional strengthening, community resilience, and reaching underserved and vulnerable populations across its operational areas in Ethiopia. Position Summary Nexus Ethiopia invites applications from highly qualified, experienced, and results-oriented professionals for the position of Communications and Digital Media Specialist. The position holder will lead the organization's communications and digital media functions, including website management and technical enhancement, social media management, news production, multimedia content development, branding, and organizational and donor visibility. The successful candidate must possess both strong professional qualifications in communications and digital media and demonstrated technical expertise in website development and management. The position requires an individual capable of independently managing the organization's digital platforms while producing high-quality communication materials that enhance Nexus Ethiopia's institutional profile, programme visibility, partnership engagement, and public outreach. Key Duties and Responsibilities A. Website Management and Technical Development Manage, maintain, and regularly update the official Nexus Ethiopia website. Lead website enhancement, redesign, development, and functionality improvements to ensure a modern, professional, secure, responsive, and user-friendly platform. Develop and maintain website pages, content management systems, multimedia features, and other digital components. Troubleshoot website-related technical issues, improve performance, and ensure compatibility across devices and browsers. Apply appropriate website security, backup, accessibility, search engine optimization (SEO), and data protection practices. Monitor website traffic and user engagement and recommend improvements based on performance analytics. Ensure that the website accurately reflects the organization's mandate, programmes, geographical coverage, achievements, partnerships, publications, and strategic priorities. B. Social Media and Digital Communications Manage Nexus Ethiopia's official social media accounts and digital communication platforms. Develop and implement a social media strategy and content calendar aligned with organizational priorities. Create, edit, and publish engaging digital content, including graphics, infographics, short videos, and multimedia posts. Monitor social media engagement, audience growth, reach, and performance and prepare periodic analytics reports. Strengthen the organization's digital presence and engagement with donors, partners, government institutions, civil society organizations, and the public. C. News, Publications, and Organizational Storytelling Write, edit, and publish organizational news, press releases, newsletters, success stories, human-interest stories, case studies, and programme updates. Document programme achievements, community experiences, lessons learned, and good practices in collaboration with programme and field teams. Translate technical humanitarian, development, and peacebuilding information into clear and compelling communication products. Prepare and update organizational profiles, brochures, annual reports, presentations, fact sheets, and other institutional publications. Ensure the accuracy, consistency, quality, and timely publication of all communication materials. D. Branding, Visibility, and Donor Communications Ensure consistent application of Nexus Ethiopia's branding and corporate identity across all communication products. Design and produce professional communication materials, including reports, presentations, banners, brochures, digital publications, and promotional materials. Ensure compliance with donor visibility requirements and partnership communication obligations. Support visibility activities for project launches, workshops, field visits, campaigns, and other organizational events. Develop communication materials that demonstrate organizational achievements, programme impact, partnerships, and contributions to local humanitarian response and sustainable development. E. Multimedia Production and Documentation Produce and edit photographs, videos, interviews, digital stories, and other multimedia products. Coordinate with programme teams and field offices to collect quality photographs, videos, testimonials, and programme documentation. Maintain an organized digital repository of photographs, videos, publications, and communication materials. Ensure informed consent, confidentiality, safeguarding, and ethical representation of communities, particularly children and vulnerable populations. F. Strategic Communications and Coordination Contribute to the development and implementation of the organization's communications and visibility strategy. Work closely with management, programme, partnership, and resource mobilization teams to identify and communicate organizational achievements and opportunities. Support the preparation of communication packages for proposals, donor engagement, partnership development, and institutional events. Monitor communications performance and prepare periodic reports on website functionality, digital engagement, visibility, and communication outputs. Perform other relevant duties assigned by the Executive Director.",
