    "description": "Vacancy Announcement MSD is an indigenous, non-profit civil society organization established in 1999 with a mission to improve the health, well-being, and socio-economic conditions of communities across Ethiopia. Over the past decades, MSD has evolved into a well-established development and humanitarian organization , delivering evidence-based, community-centered programs that respond to the evolving needs of vulnerable and underserved populations. MSD implements integrated programs across a broad range of thematic areas, including: Health and Nutrition: TB, HIV/AIDS, sexual and reproductive health (SRH), maternal, newborn and child health (MNCH), and nutrition. Education and Skills Development: Access to quality education, technical and vocational education and training (TVET), and skills development. Social Mobilization and Livelihoods: Economic strengthening, community mobilization, and prevention of harmful traditional practices (HTPs), gender-based violence (GBV), and female genital mutilation (FGM), Migration and Trafficking: Safe migration, protection, rehabilitation, and reintegration support for migrants, returnees, and victims of trafficking; Child Care and Development: Child protection, early childhood care and development, and infant and young child feeding. , Human Rights and Good Governance: Democratization, peace building, social accountability, civic engagement, and dialogue; Humanitarian and Emergency Response: Integrated assistance and protection services for communities affected by conflict, displacement, disasters, and other emergencies; and Environment and Climate Change: Environmental sustainability, climate resilience, and biodiversity conservation. Through these integrated programs, MSD works in close collaboration with federal and regional government institutions, communities, civil society organizations, development and humanitarian partners, and other stakeholders to strengthen local systems, expand access to essential services, promote inclusion and equity, and build resilient communities across Ethiopia. Project Background: MSD, with financial support from UNICEF, will implement a five-month project (November 1, 2026–March 31, 2027) entitled “Enhancing Access to Life-Saving Protection and Gender-Based Violence Services for Women and Girls in Conflict-Affected and Humanitarian Settings” in Wogera, Lay Gayint, and Simada Woredas of Amhara Region. The project aims to strengthen access to essential child protection and GBV prevention and response services by reaching 480 vulnerable children with protection and cash assistance, identifying and reunifying 99 unaccompanied and separated children, and providing emergency assistance to 174 GBV survivors. It will also establish and strengthen six Women and Girls' Safe Spaces (WGSS), six Child-Friendly Spaces (CFS), equip three health facilities/One-Stop Centers (OSCs) with Clinical Management of Rape (CMR) and dignity supplies, and strengthen 30 Community-Based Child Protection Structures (CBCPS).\" MSD is looking for qualified and competent applicants for the following position: Position: M&E Specialist Location: Bahirdar Salary: Negotiable subject to organizational salary scale and project budget No. Required: 1 Gender: Both male and female are invited, and women are highly encouraged to apply. Term of Employment: Contract JOB SUMMARY Monitoring and Evaluation officer is a position in the organization with the overall responsibility of developing monitoring plan, consolidating, document, track and update M&E data as well as ensuring the data is of the best quality possible. She/he will continuously engage in supervising performance of the project against the plan, providing technical assistance to project staffs, and coordinate periodic performance review, site level JISS with the relevant stakeholders. SPECIFIC DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Monitoring project activities, outputs and progress towards anticipated results and working with data platforms, databases and select technologies to capture and organize data Facilitating the input of project staff, partners and other stakeholders in project design and measurement activities. Participating in and providing support to project design activities including development of project theories of change and strategic frameworks (Results Frameworks, Log Frames and result chain) Develop and implement monitoring and evaluation frameworks/plans to assess; and track project progress, outcomes and effectiveness against the intended goal and objectives ; Undertake continuous data management (data cleaning, sorting, categorizing and organizing data quality assessments, Analysis and Reporting) and quality assurance per donor requirement and organization standard and guideline; Determining data analysis procedures and use of quantitative or qualitative analysis tools Prepares monthly, quarterly, biannual and annual financial and project performance reports of the project and submit to organization and donor per the designated timeline. Put in place a monitoring system to collect baseline and periodic data for tracking project performance and decision making; Periodically conduct monitoring, JISS, review meeting with staffs, regional and sub-regional stakeholders. Maintain project documents, lessons and innovations as part of knowledge management. Provide support to knowledge management processes within the organizations and Contributing to institutional learning processes",
